<Base title="Engineering — Maheswaran" description="Thermal-fluid and CFD engineering across engines, batteries, electric vehicles, vehicle systems and system simulation.">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Engineering</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:52px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:10px 0 18px">Physics first. Simulation in service of decisions.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#666;max-width:820px">My engineering focus is thermal and flow physics across multiple applications — engines and powertrain, batteries and electric vehicles, complete vehicle thermal management and aerodynamics, and system-level simulation. Combustion is one important part of that landscape, not the boundary of it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid">
    <article id="engine" class="topic"><h3>Engine & powertrain</h3><ul><li>Thermal management</li><li>Combustion CFD & CHT</li><li>Air-path / manifolds</li><li>Alternative fuels</li><li>Cooling & heat rejection</li></ul></article>
    <article id="thermal" class="topic"><h3>Thermal & CHT</h3><ul><li>Conjugate heat transfer</li><li>Cooling passages</li><li>Heat rejection</li><li>Transient thermal behaviour</li><li>Thermal validation</li></ul></article>
    <article id="battery" class="topic"><h3>Battery & electric vehicle</h3><ul><li>Cell / pack thermal</li><li>Cooling architectures</li><li>Thermal runaway & propagation</li><li>E-drive / electronics thermal</li><li>Electro-thermal systems</li></ul></article>
    <article id="vehicle" class="topic"><h3>Vehicle & flow systems</h3><ul><li>External aerodynamics</li><li>Vehicle thermal management</li><li>HVAC</li><li>Cooling airflow</li><li>Underhood / underbody flow</li></ul></article>
  </div></section>

  <section id="systems" class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">System simulation</div><h2>1D / system-level modelling</h2>
    <div class="card"><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.7">Modelica, GT-Suite style system thinking, reduced models, CFD–1D coupling, thermal networks and energy-flow studies belong here. The goal is to connect component-level physics to complete-system decisions.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>